Like I stated earlier one way that the boulder can get there is during 
the level creation. I just checked the source and there is no reason why 
the following couldn't happen.

During the trap creation a pit is created. When further traps are 
created a rolling boulder trap is created. When the boulder for the trap 
is created there is no check that the boulder cannot be created in a pit 
location and if it is it's not dropped into the pit.

mkroll_launch() (trap.c line 1559) =>
	isclearpath() (two calls lines 1586 and 1590)
	mksobj() (call on line 1603)
	place_object() (call on line 1606)
	stackobj() (call on line 1607)

isclearpath() (trap.c line 1621)
	Only checks that location is ok (not out of bounds), can be zapped 
trough and is not a closed door.

mksobj() (mkobj.c line 363)
	Only creates an item, does not place it anywhere. That has to be done 
by the caller explicitely and mkroll_launch() uses place_object()

place_object() (mkobj.c line 1101)
	Just puts the item on the floor location linked lists without any other 
check than these three:
		1. Boulder placed on the floor blocks vision.
		2. Items go under a boulder if there is one on the locatioin.
		3. Timed items get their timers checked.

stackobj() (invent.c line 2309)
	Just merges mergable items on the same location.

So I'm quite sure that the boulder was a boulder of a rolling boulder trap.

